A||||12||Alex4mula||Not better after increase fuel preasure..||||5||
Z||000000||Alex4mula||06-28-2000||02:10 PM||||Took 1st measure of fuel preasure after installing 3.4 engine with FPR. It was showing 30 PSI which is low but car was running OK. Adjusted it to 40 PSI & now I feel the car is holding, or feels not reving as fast as before. It revs smoothly to 6.3K rpm. Before I oil change only took it to 4K. Car has driven near 600 miles before changing oil & making this adjustment. It is an 88 Formula stick just in case. Any suggestions?||||reg||5
Z||000001||1FST2M6||06-28-2000||02:31 PM||||take it to a local Dynojet shop and see if your over fueling it! to much fuel will cause the car to rev slow... <A HREF="http://www.dynojet.com" TARGET=_blank>www.dynojet.com</A>  do you have an air/fuel meter? teh shop has one with injector duty cycle and air/fuel for like $130. which will tell you if you really do need more fuel or different injectors... <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||ThatRickGuy||06-28-2000||03:20 PM||||1FST2M6 is right, this is one of the place's where More's law doesn't always apply (More is better) Fuel burns optimally at 16:1 (16 parts air, 1 part fuel) so, it's all about getting more of the proper mixture, too far one way, and you'll start to ping, too far the other, and you'll just get horride performance. Take it to a dyno shop and let them tweak it, they know how to get the numbers right.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Alex4mula||06-28-2000||07:39 PM||||My AutoXray scanner shows rich (0.9-1.0V at O2) all the way up to 6.3K rpm. I am using stock 2.8 injectors. I know about the Dyno but haven't been able to locate one near my area (WPB, FL). What I don't understand is how it may be putting more than needed fuel at 40 PSI which is even lower than the 43 PSI that the stock regulator should supply. And just in case I know that the gage is OK because I used it to mesure with the previous engine/injectors/rail combination. Anything else to check?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cooter||06-28-2000||08:14 PM||||My 3.4 with the factory 3.4 injectors and 88 ECM runs around 800mv at full throttle. I have not checked the fuel pressure yet, but will tomorrow because you have got me curious now.||||reg||1
Z||000005||ThatRickGuy||06-28-2000||10:44 PM||||Alex,<BR> 40 psi one a 2 inch wide pipe is a lot more then 43 psi on a 1 inch pipe. exageration in sizes there, but my guess would be that the 3.4 injectors may run a little smaller, w/ higher preasure, IOW less fuel gets in, but it's mixing with the air better. I'd say try backing it off little by little, you won't be able to get it exact, but you should be able to get it to pick up a little better. also, I'm not sure if the computerized cars have them or not, but on older beasts there are weights and springs that work w/ the distributer and rotor. heavier weights, lighter springs will make the mechanical advance come out faster thus decreasing your rev time, but be carful, too light and al of a sudden you'll be idleing at 3000rpm.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Alex4mula||06-29-2000||10:00 AM||||Mine runs from 900 to 1000 mV (i.e. 1V) at full throtle. Injector pulse is 10 to 11ms at above readings. Remember that I am using 2.8 injectors, not the 3.4s. Will try to decrease presure and check readings again. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||1FST2M6||06-29-2000||12:47 PM||||13.8:1 is what i learned in ICT 1101/05 (Internal Combustion Theory at Ga. Tech Professer/Dr. S. Brewer) <P>anyway.. have you had the injectors cleaned? are you sure there is no carbon or varnish on/in them causing them to react incorrectly. and since they are just a simple coil their age alone may play a factor. with age/heat/and weather the impedance of the coil will change making them react poorly sticking open to long etc... just one more thing to think about...  Thats crappy about no local Dynojet... humm feel like driving to Atl?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I've got a spare room if you need a place to crash. have to be after the 12th of july though. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Alex4mula||06-29-2000||01:21 PM||||1ST,<BR>Injectors were sent to Marren motorsports last fall for blueprinting/flow match. I'm sure that at Daytona there must be a dyno. Less far than Atlanta but still 3.5 hrs drive. Thanks for the offer anyway. <P>Cooter; Are you using a FPR?||||reg||1
Z||000009||1FST2M6||06-29-2000||01:26 PM||||Dynojet themselves takes a mobile 248C to Daytona all the time! (Raceway) not sure about their ability to do any tuning or exhaust gas analyzing onsite though. e-mail them ... Stillen, Vortech, Weapon-R, AEM and Jackson Racing all make FPR that will work on our cars... I've had a Stillen unit and now have an FMU (doesn't do anything unless under boost/nitrous)||||reg||1
